## Terraform

{% if backend == 'datadog' %}
Export Datadog credentials before `terraform init` / `plan` / `apply`:

```bash
export DD_API_KEY="<your-api-key>"
export DD_APP_KEY="<your-application-key>"
```

The [Datadog Terraform provider](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/DataDog/datadog/latest/docs)
reads `DD_API_KEY` and `DD_APP_KEY` from the environment. Application keys need
monitor write scope for the generated `datadog_monitor` resources. The provider sets
`validate = false` so `terraform plan` works in CI without keys; live apply still requires
valid credentials.

Monitor messages reference **{{ notification_target }}**; wire PagerDuty or Slack in
Datadog monitor notifications after apply.
{% elif backend == 'grafana' %}
Set `GRAFANA_AUTH` or provider URL/auth per [Grafana provider docs](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/grafana/grafana/latest/docs).
{% elif backend == 'prometheus' %}
Terraform mode does **not** call a Prometheus API. `prometheus_rules.tf` and `alertmanager.tf`
embed starter rule and routing YAML in `null_resource` triggers. Export those payloads in your
pipeline to the ruler and Alertmanager configs you operate (Mimir, AMP, Prometheus Operator, etc.).
{% elif backend == 'otel' %}
Configure kubeconfig/Helm provider auth per your cluster standard before `terraform apply`.
{% endif %}

Regenerate gates include `terraform-fmt`, `terraform-validate`, `opa` (plan or vendored fixture),
and `secrets` when the toolchain is installed.
{% endif %}

